# SaaS

## Tenancy

The tenant comes from the authenticated session and nowhere else. No header, no
query parameter, no body field influences which tenant a request is bound to.

## Entitlements are data

Never `if (plan === 'PRO')`. Ask `entitlements.allows('SAFETY_MODULE')` or
`assertWithinLimit(entitlements, 'MAX_USERS', count)`.

A missing entitlement is **402**, not 403 — "your plan does not include this" and
"you are not allowed to do this" are different problems with different fixes.

Adding a feature flag means adding an `EntitlementKey` and granting it in the
plan catalogue, not a code branch.

## Roles are data too

Never branch on a role name. Ask for a permission, so a customer's custom role
behaves exactly like a built-in one.

## Per-tenant everything

Settings, branding, warning ladders, renewal intervals, notification policy and
disclaimers are the organization's own configuration. OLBOS never hard-codes a
regulatory default and never implies one.
